{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qhjjz7q6vacsoz6hmcllyf7cfwnzcpvxxpju2fnbmmlhrnktea6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01HjsKhWDFVJc7QRZHQ7wVAn","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit C vs Rust line by line","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are auditing a C-to-Rust translation for EXACT behavioral equivalence. Do NOT modify any files. Report findings only.\n\nFiles (absolute paths):\n- C ground truth: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KkkAp8/c_src/src/lib.c   (969 lines)\n- Rust translation: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KkkAp8/translation/src/lib.rs\n\nThis is a subset of the `stb_ds` library (dynamic arrays + hash maps + a string arena) plus `strkey`/`str_dups`.\n\nRead BOTH files IN FULL. Then perform a meticulous, function-by-function, statement-by-statement comparison of every function. The C is ALWAYS correct — report any place where the Rust would produce a different observable result for ANY input, including pathological ones.\n\nPay very close attention to:\n1. C integer promotion / usual arithmetic conversions, and sign extension. e.g. `d[3] << 24` where `d` is `unsigned char*` promotes to `int`, may become negative, and is then sign-extended when assigned/OR'd into a `size_t`. Verify EVERY such site in `stbds_siphash_bytes` (the main loop AND the fall-through `switch (len - i)` tail) and in `stbds_hash_string`.\n2. The `stbds_load_32_or_64` macro expansions in `stbds_make_hash_index` (the `a` and `b` multiplier constants). Check the C type of each literal: `0x87b0b0fd` and `0xb504f32d` do not fit in `int` so they are `unsigned int`; `2147001325` and `715136305` do fit so they are `int`. Verify the Rust reproduces the exact same zero/sign extension.\n3. Evaluation order and the exact set of fields written, in `stbds_hmput_key` (especially the two inner probe loops: which one writes `hash_table->temp_key` and which one does NOT), `stbds_hmdel_key`, `stbds_hmget_key_ts`, `stbds_hmput_default`, `stbds_shmode_func`.\n4. Off-by-one and index base: `stbds_header`, `STBDS_HASH_TO_ARR`/`STBDS_ARR_TO_HASH`, `bucket->index[..] = i-1`, `length = i+1`, `final_index = arrlen(raw_a)-1-1`.\n5. Every comparison operator: `>=` vs `==` vs `>` (e.g. `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` vs `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING`), `<` vs `<=`.\n6. `stbds_stralloc`: `512u << (block>>1)`, the `++a->block` gate, the two oversized-block splice branches, and the final `p = storage + remaining - len` arithmetic.\n7. `stbds_strreset`, `stbds_hmfree_func` (which indices it frees, starting index).\n8. `stbds_arrgrowf`: the order of the three min_cap adjustments, and which fields are initialized only when `a == NULL`.\n9. `str_dups` and `strkey`: exact format strings, the `shputs`/`sh_new_strdup`/`shfree` macro expansions, the `stbds_hmlen` (`length - 1`) computation, and the `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)` call where a 16-byte struct is passed BY VALUE through varargs.\n10. All 10 `STBDS_ASSERT` sites in the C — verify the Rust has an equivalent check with the IDENTICAL condition (note: `assert` is LIVE in the C build; it is not compiled out).\n\nFor each function, state explicitly either \"MATCHES\" or describe the precise divergence with C line numbers, Rust line numbers, and a concrete input that would expose it.\n\nFinish with a numbered list of concrete divergences (or \"NO DIVERGENCES FOUND\"). Be rigorous and skeptical; do not hand-wave."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4659,"cache_read_input_tokens":332499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4659,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ccbcf35-f98e-4533-a9d0-8fa1633f055f","uuid":"7163b4b6-c53e-4367-9395-abf145dd2242","timestamp":"2026-08-27T18:30:51.286Z"}
