{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yt3cn57hqsi6a2pgzet7fql36letvcgoggwkgtsekeuvcyh33m6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass under every configuration.\n\n## What the code is\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is a subset of `stb_ds` — growable arrays, an open-addressed hash map with three string-key ownership modes (`SH_DEFAULT`/`SH_STRDUP`/`SH_ARENA`), a string arena, and the `strkey`/`str_dups` drivers. The public header declares only `str_dups`, but the translation unit exports **16** symbols; all 16 are in scope.\n\n## Three real defects found and fixed\n\n1. **All ten `STBDS_ASSERT`s were missing from the Rust.** `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no build type → no `-DNDEBUG`, and `nm -D` on the C `.so` confirms `U __assert_fail`: assertions are **live**. Most are unreachable, but `STBDS_ASSERT(slot >= 0)` at `lib.c:846` **is** reachable — via `hmdel_key` with a non-zero `keyoffset`, and via any `mode >= 2` on a string map (line 845 then hashes the *address* of the moved element). Where C stopped hard, the Rust was computing `storage.offset(-1)` and writing `b->index[7]` into the `hash_index` header: silent memory corruption. Comparing this needed a fork-per-implementation harness (`diff_child`), since the first abort otherwise kills the test runner.\n\n2. **Rust's debug-only UB checks changed behavior.** `stbds_hash_string(NULL, seed)` gives SIGSEGV in C but SIGABRT from rustc's injected null-deref check; the same check turned C's legal-on-x86 *unaligned* `char*` store (any `elemsize` not a multiple of 8) into an abort. `Cargo.toml` now disables `debug-assertions`/`overflow-checks` for `dev`/`test`, and the suite runs against **both** the debug and release `.so`.\n\n3. **The suite could have passed vacuously.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target — editing `src/lib.rs` left the `.so` byte-identical (md5-verified), and my first mutation run scored **0/10** purely because of this. `tests/common/mod.rs::assert_fresh()` now hard-fails on a stale `.so`.\n\n## Gate\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` diff **empty both ways**, 16/16; 0 undefined non-libc symbols; no stubs |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **64/64** rows pass (55 derived up front + 9 added during testing) |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **60/60** rows have a passing error-path test (52 test fns) |\n| Feature combos | crate declares **no** features (`cargo metadata` → `features: {}`); `run_all_configs.sh` enumerates the powerset mechanically and adds the dev×release profile axis |\n| Total | **120 tests**, green against both the debug and release cdylib |\n\nComparison is address-independent: full array header + `hash_index` + **every bucket's `hash[8]`/`index[8]`** + element bytes/key strings, `stralloc` results as `(block chain index, offset)`, `str_dups` stdout via `dup2`, and termination signals for abort paths.\n\n## Sensitivity proven, not assumed\n\n`mutation_check.py`: **33 caught / 5 survivors, 0 unexplained** — survivors are behaviorally equivalent (e.g. the `slot_count > 8` shrink clause is dead because `shrink_threshold` is forced to 0 at `slot_count == 8`) or memory-only effects invisible through a `void` API. One survivor was a genuine gap — the `len == blocksize` boundary in `stralloc` — now closed by `cfg18b` (row 18b).\n\nBehavior deliberately **not** \"fixed\": the `temp_key` refresh asymmetry between `hmput_key`'s two probe loops (which makes `shputs` + `SH_STRDUP` double-free upstream), the `512u << (block>>1)` shift-count UB, the siphash `int` sign-extension, and `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], ...)` passing a 16-byte struct through varargs. `c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":993,"cache_read_input_tokens":458192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":993,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ccbcf35-f98e-4533-a9d0-8fa1633f055f","uuid":"d593ff78-4bab-4ea9-bb2f-be47d04af391","timestamp":"2026-08-27T19:16:32.301Z"}
